  "body": "What happens:\n- A band of a whole-model 2D contour has two outer rings.\n- Only one of the two rings has a floor level.\n- The note for the ring without a floor level is dropped.\n- The region of that ring stays uncut.\n- The result has no note for that region.\n- This happens in band 0 and in an in-between band.\n\nWhere:\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_whole.rs`, the band-0 arm and the in-between band.\n- Present since commit ceac40dd9. Also in merge 6a3e211f2.\n- Found in the review of PR #2460 (issue #2436), comment 6980642597.\n\nExpected:\n- Each uncut region gets a visible note or an error.\n- A silent wrong result breaks the Prime Directive in AGENTS.md.\n\nDone means:\n- A test in `crates/motion/tests/contour_whole.rs` pins a part with two outer rings.\n- One of the two rings has no floor level.\n- The result names the uncut Z range of that ring.\n\nFollow-up of PR #2460 (issue #2436).\n",
